@@ -10,7 +10,8 @@ and TypeScript declarations in `dist`.
 `createRentalService()` is exported from `src/index.ts`. Each service holds its own equipment and
 bookings in memory. Register boards and sails with `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })`, then use
 `quote({ itemId, start, end })` or `book({ itemId, start, end })`. Booking IDs are unique within a service.
-Equipment IDs cannot be registered twice. Prices must be non-negative safe integers in euro cents;
+An optional `hourlyPrice` sets the cost of one hour of rental. Equipment IDs cannot be registered twice.
+Prices must be non-negative safe integers in euro cents;
 totals must also fit in a safe integer.
 
 Periods use ISO-8601 UTC midnight timestamps, such as `2026-06-10T00:00:00Z` (an explicit `+00:00`
@@ -18,6 +19,10 @@ offset is also accepted). The end must be after the start and is exclusive: June
 costs two daily prices. Adjacent bookings are allowed. Quotes do not reserve equipment or check
 availability; booking rejects any overlap for the same item. Unknown items and invalid periods throw.
 
+Rentals shorter than 24 hours may start and end on any whole hour in UTC and cost the hourly price
+for each hour, including periods that cross midnight. These rentals require an `hourlyPrice` on the
+item. Rentals of 24 hours or more still require midnight endpoints and use the daily price.
+
 Rentals of three days or more receive 10% off the full rental price in both quotes and bookings.
 The reduced total is rounded once to the nearest cent, with half cents rounded up. The full price
 must still fit in a safe integer before the discount is applied.
@@ -25,6 +30,7 @@ must still fit in a safe integer before the discount is applied.
 Use `availability({ start, end, kind? })` to list equipment free for the whole period, optionally
 filtered to `board` or `sail`. It returns equipment IDs in lexicographic order, uses the same period
 validation and exclusive end as booking, and does not reserve equipment. Invalid kinds throw.
+For rentals shorter than 24 hours, it only includes items with an hourly price.
 
 Cancellation is not implemented yet. The school's policy for future implementation is: cancellation
 less than 24 hours before the booking starts gives no refund; otherwise the full amount is refunded.
